# `backend/**/*` Rules (sample)

> This file is a sample with the `.example` extension. Activate by copying without the extension:
> ```bash
> cp .claude/rules/path-backend.md.example .claude/rules/path-backend.md
> ```
>
> Edit to fit your project. Delete sections you don't need.

## Scope

These rules apply when editing files under `backend/**/*`.
They do not apply to frontend or mobile code.

## Layer structure

Assumed layering (adjust to your project):

```text
backend/
├── api/          # HTTP handlers / routing
├── services/     # Business logic
├── repositories/ # Data access
├── domain/       # Entities / value objects
├── infra/        # DB connection, external services
└── tests/        # Tests
```

## Dependency direction rules

- `api` → `services` → `repositories` → `domain` + `infra`
- Reverse dependencies are forbidden (`domain` must not call `services`)
- Sibling dependencies within `infra` are forbidden
- No circular dependencies

Detection command examples (adjust per language):

```bash
# TypeScript
npx depcruise backend --config

# Python
pydeps backend --show-deps
```

## API design

- Endpoints follow REST conventions (`POST /resources`, `GET /resources/:id`, etc.)
- JSON responses. Structured errors: `{ error: { code, message, details } }`
- Cursor-based pagination (avoid offset/limit)
- Version via URL path (`/v1/`, `/v2/`)

## Authentication / authorization

- Authentication at the API gateway layer (api)
- Authorization at the use-case layer (services)
- Tokens via headers. Never via query parameters
- JWT secrets / API keys via env vars (`${JWT_SECRET}`)

## Database

- Migrations managed by a dedicated tool (Prisma / SQLAlchemy Alembic / Flyway)
- Destructive production migrations (DROP COLUMN, etc.) run in two phases (1. stop writes → 2. drop)
- Transaction boundaries explicit at the services layer

## Error handling

- Distinguish domain exceptions from technical exceptions
- Convert to HTTP status codes at the api layer
- Structured (JSON) log output
- Stack traces are not included in production responses

## Performance

- Detect N+1 queries in dev mode
- Timeouts mandatory for outbound service calls
- Long-running work moves to async jobs (via queue)

## Security

- All input validated (at domain / services boundaries)
- SQL is always parameterized
- File uploads: size / type checks, path traversal prevention
- See `@.claude/pitfalls.md` Security section for more

## Tests

- Unit: services / domain-focused
- Integration: api-layer end-to-end with real DB (sqlite / testcontainers)
- E2E: api + external service mocks
- Coverage targets follow `project-config.md` §6

## Concept alignment

- This is a path-specific rule and does not affect frontend code
- Project-wide architecture pattern lives in `project-config.md` §4
- Concrete tech choices live in `project-config.md` §2
